Author: huangqibo <huangqibo@xiaomi.com> (Xiaomi), feature "MiSight_LogEnhance".

Match with stock amethyst miev.ko (OS3.0.306.0, vendor_boot):
  same module name, author and description; the same five exports
  (cdev_tevent_alloc/add_int/add_str/write/destroy); the same function set
  (write_buf_inner, check_work, do_miev_work, miev_get_work_msg,
  miev_release_work_msg, write_kbuf, miev_{open,release,read,write,poll,ioctl})
  and the same log strings. The driver has no SoC-specific code, so the
  MediaTek-tree copy is the driver the Qualcomm build uses.
  The older MiCode copy (Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource socrates-t-oss,
  drivers/staging/miev) uses a linked-list payload layout and was not used.

Changes: none to the C sources or headers. Kbuild and Makefile replace the
release's Kconfig/Makefile. Kbuild defines CONFIG_MIEV_MODULE=1 so that
include/miev/mievent.h exposes the real prototypes.
